[Event "Dragon: Yugoslav Attack 9.Bc4"]
[Opening "Sicilian Dragon"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 c5 {The Sicilian: fight for d4 from the side.} 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 {Trade your side pawn for White's center pawn.} 4. Nxd4 Nf6 {Attack e4.} 5. Nc3 g6 {The Dragon! Your bishop will breathe fire on the long diagonal.} 6. Be3 Bg7 7. f3 O-O 8. Qd2 Nc6 9. Bc4 {The Yugoslav Attack: White will castle long and storm your king.} Bd7 10. O-O-O Rc8 {Your rook goes to the open c-file – that is where YOUR attack is.} 11. Bb3 Ne5 {The knight heads for c4.} 12. h4 h5 {Stop White's h-pawn. Both sides race to attack!} *

[Event "Dragon: Yugoslav 9.O-O-O d5!"]
[Opening "Sicilian Dragon"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be3 Bg7 7. f3 O-O 8. Qd2 Nc6 9. O-O-O d5 {Strike in the center at once! This is the best way to fight White's attack.} 10. exd5 Nxd5 11. Nxc6 bxc6 12. Bd4 e5 {Kick the bishop.} 13. Bc5 Be6 {Develop with tempo. Your pieces are very active.} *

[Event "Dragon: Classical 6.Be2"]
[Opening "Sicilian Dragon"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be2 {Calm: White castles short.} Bg7 7. O-O O-O 8. Be3 Nc6 9. Nb3 Be6 {Develop and look at the queen side.} 10. f4 Rc8 {Rook to the c-file. Equal and comfortable for you.} *

[Event "Dragon: Levenfish 6.f4"]
[Opening "Sicilian Dragon"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. f4 {Careful! After 6...Bg7? comes 7.e5 with a strong attack.} Nbd7 {The safe move: this knight guards e5.} 7. Nf3 Bg7 8. Bd3 O-O 9. O-O Nc5 {Now everything is safe and your knight is active.} *

[Event "Dragon: 6.Bc4"]
[Opening "Sicilian Dragon"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Bc4 {The bishop aims at f7.} Bg7 7. O-O O-O 8. h3 Nc6 9. Be3 Nxe4 {The fork trick! You take e4 …} 10. Nxe4 d5 {… and win the piece back with a pawn fork. Equal game and your pieces are free.} *

[Event "Sicilian (Black): Smith-Morra Accepted"]
[Opening "Sicilian: White's other tries"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 c5 2. d4 {The Smith-Morra Gambit.} cxd4 3. c3 dxc3 {Take the pawn – you are a pawn up.} 4. Nxc3 Nc6 5. Nf3 d6 {Solid: keep White's knight out of b5 and d5 later.} 6. Bc4 e6 {Close the diagonal to f7.} 7. O-O Nf6 8. Qe2 Be7 {Get ready to castle.} 9. Rd1 e5 {Block the d-file in front of your queen.} 10. h3 O-O {King safe and a pawn up. Good for Black.} *

[Event "Trap (Black): The Siberian Trap"]
[Opening "Sicilian: White's other tries"]
[Side "Black"]
[Check "trap"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 c5 2. d4 {The Smith-Morra Gambit.} cxd4 3. c3 dxc3 {Take the pawn!} 4. Nxc3 Nc6 5. Nf3 e6 6. Bc4 Qc7 {A bit risky (7.Nb5! is annoying), but it sets the trap: your queen looks at h2.} 7. O-O Nf6 8. Qe2 Ng4 {Threatens ...Nd4 and ...Qh2.} 9. h3 {A mistake! Now comes the Siberian Trap.} Nd4 {Attack the queen!} 10. Nxd4 {If White takes the knight …} Qh2# {… checkmate! The queen lands on h2.} *

[Event "Sicilian (Black): Alapin 2.c3"]
[Opening "Sicilian: White's other tries"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 c5 2. c3 {The Alapin: White wants d4 with a pawn.} Nf6 {Hit e4 right away.} 3. e5 Nd5 4. d4 cxd4 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. cxd4 d6 {Attack the e5 pawn.} 7. Bc4 Nb6 8. Bb5 dxe5 9. Nxe5 Bd7 {Good development. Equal game.} *

[Event "Sicilian (Black): 3.Bb5+"]
[Opening "Sicilian: White's other tries"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bb5+ {A check to avoid the main lines.} Bd7 {Block and offer a trade.} 4. Bxd7+ Qxd7 5. O-O Nc6 6. c3 Nf6 7. Re1 e6 {Solid. Next ...Be7 and castle.} 8. d4 cxd4 9. cxd4 d5 {Hit the center. Equal game.} *

[Event "Sicilian (Black): Grand Prix 2.Nc3 3.f4"]
[Opening "Sicilian: White's other tries"]
[Side "Black"]
[Result "*"]

1. e4 c5 2. Nc3 Nc6 3. f4 {The Grand Prix Attack: White attacks on the king side.} g6 {Fianchetto – your bishop will be strong.} 4. Nf3 Bg7 5. Bc4 e6 {Close the diagonal to f7.} 6. f5 Nge7 {Develop and watch f5.} 7. fxe6 dxe6 8. d3 O-O *

